exec
/bin/zsh -lc "cat > evidence/NEEDS.md <<'EOF'
# Coldsmoke Tuning — local acceptance

Builder's local review, not an independent review. Real Chrome screenshots use phone (390×844 and 844×390), wall (1440×900) and staff tablet (1024×768) viewports. These are browser-emulated phone surfaces, not a physical handset test.

| Maya's need | Result | Evidence / limits |
|---|---|---|
| Customers book from a phone and open real Stripe payment | Met in sandbox | "'`phone-stripe-payment-link.png`; actual buy.stripe.com link; `acceptance.json` matches local order to Stripe Checkout client_reference_id. |
| Seat secured only when paid | Met in sandbox | Pending record before payment; tok_visa API confirmation succeeded for CAD 60; signed webhook made it confirmed. `phone-pending.png`, `phone-paid.png`. No browser card entry. |
| Pending is best effort and does not block another guest | Met | Two separate browser contexts opened the same capacity-one slot before either paid; two different local booking IDs recorded. No unpaid exclusive hold. |
| Workshop wall shows bookings and payment updates | Met locally | Original ski rail scene; `wall-pending.png`, `wall-paid.png`, `wall-moved.png`; public data contains only slot, state, quantity and reference. Two-second polling. |
| Full slot refuses another booking | Met | Disabled Full button and direct purchase rejection, HTTP 409; `phone-full.png` and JSON receipt. Stripe completed-session limit is one. |
| Staff publish slots, then owner AI syncs | Met locally | Staff UI publication, complete manifest from records, native Payment Links from authorized helper. `staff-published.png`, `.studio/booking-slots.json`, acceptance source. Local test staff session; production passkey ceremony not exercised. |
| Staff move paid bookings safely | Met locally, operational caveat | UI move v2→v3; stale v2 update rejected with 409. `staff-moved.png`. Owner must review/resync affected links after moves; this was not treated as an automatic capacity transfer. |
| Public cannot operate staff controls | Met for tested write | Public slot creation refused with 403. Server permissions are enforced; UI role parameter alone is not authority. |
| Returning customer sees their booking | Met using explicit tracking link | Fresh context, page reload, all contexts closed and reopened; `phone-return.png`, `phone-landscape.png`. Copy-link clipboard behavior is browser dependent; ordinary bare-page auto-recovery is not guaranteed in the sandboxed frame. |
| Generic homie-studio check | See generic-check.json | Isolated role/slot needs plus intentionally unasserted payment needs; custom sandbox results above are separate evidence, not a claimed all-green generic check. |

## Real-world assumptions and gaps
- Prototype offer is CAD $60 for edges and hot wax. Maya has not supplied actual pricing, tax treatment, scope, dates/timezone, cancellation/refund policy or working capacity. Sample slots are Oct 17, 2026. Duplicate labels and abandoned pending requests in captures are test-run residue, not real customers.
- Stripe'"'s lifetime completed-session counter does not decrease after refunds or staff moves. The destination's local paid occupancy and the provider's lifetime counter are different constraints. Review and explicitly resync affected links before selling more; no capacity increment was used to conceal a full result. Post-move resync/refund lifecycle was not exercised.
- The uncompleted competing Checkout is left pending best effort. Expiry timing and an already-open competing session completing after capacity is full were not tested.
- The helper uses a disabled placeholder webhook destination and a desktop signed-event listener. Production hosting, real webhook endpoint, live Stripe activation, post-payment return address and real device reachability were not tested. No deploy/push occurred. Local QR points to loopback and is not usable by a separate physical phone.
- Workshop illustration is original CSS, not Maya's measured premises. Large queues, wall overflow, offline operation, notifications and production staff sign-in remain untested. Reduced-motion/landscape rendering was exercised; no independent usability or accessibility audit.
- The packaged shell only auto-saves hex ticket IDs, whereas bookings use "'`ord_…` IDs. Explicit tracking links work and are shown; bare URL reload may lose the selected ticket. Toolkit source was not modified.
- No media spending, live money, pasted key or alternate Stripe profile. Worker bindings were links mode plus private link/webhook settings, without STRIPE_KEY or STRIPE_API_BASE. Private binding files were removed and helper stopped at completion.
EOF
cat >> evidence/COMMANDS.md <<'"'EOF'

Acceptance troubleshooting and rerun: retained the first failed receipt, changed dotenv quoting, foregrounded Chrome pages and replaced animation-frame polling with timed DOM polling. One run was interrupted before Stripe setup after a stalled local runtime; the exact PID's cwd was verified before stopping it. Later runs reused the same unique sandbox name to retain Payment Link completion counters. Only one real sandbox payment was confirmed. A final full run passed all custom assertions, including payment, full refusal, v2→v3 staff move, stale conflict and return after all contexts closed.
EOF
